The reason why my Monks don't do very much ranged combat...

I'm going to explain the game in terms of "pre-castle" and
"post-castle".  This is because the game is much different after I have
access to the castle's wand of wishing.  I'll also explain this with
the Monk character, since that is the character I play most often.

In pre-castle, I very rarely have access to an attack spell.  This is
because of the following:
1) I rarely find a randomly generated attack spellbook. 2) I rarely
find a randomly generated magic marker, and even if I did find one,
unless I'm a wizard I'm most definitely going to use all the charges to
make enchant armor scrolls, because I'd rather have more AC than do
more ranged damage.  3) If I do get a wish in pre-castle, I have much
better things to wish for than attack spellbooks (i.e. magic
resistance, reflection, or free action).  4) I don't do long sac-fests
for spellbooks, because I'm generally missing magic resistance,
reflection, and/or free action at this point in the game, I want to get
all of those as quickly as possible because I think they are much more
important than extra damage, and exploring the dungeon has a much
higher chance of finding these items than long sac-fests.  Therefore,
ranged spells are generally not an option for me in pre-castle.

In pre-castle, I can only throw 1 projectile per turn, and these
projectiles are usually +0 or +1.  The only way the projectiles will
get boosted will be from randomly generated scrolls of enchant weapon.
As I stated above, if for some reason I am able to get hold of a magic
marker, all of those charges are going toward enchant armor scrolls,
since I think the extra AC is far more important than extra damage,
considering that I can only shoot 1 projectile per turn.  Therefore, my
martial arts damage is going to be far greater than my ranged damage.

Also keep in mind that my Monks have an extra thing to worry about,
which is starving because they don't eat meat.  Since my Monks don't
eat meat, I need to progress through the game at a fairly quick rate so
that I don't starve.  Since my ranged damage isn't very good, if I used
ranged weapons against monsters that I could melee instead, then I am
wasting valuable turns, not only because I'm doing cruddy damage, but
also because I have to waste turns to pick up the projectiles.  I'd
much rather take small amounts of melee damage, than risk starvation.
I basically worry about starvation until I reach the Castle, reach
Ludious, or get a ring of slow digestion.

So I've just discussed why I use primarly melee damage in pre-castle.
In post-castle, the extra damage of ranged attacks is just overkill.
Seriously, my AC is so low at that point of the game, that I could
melee 90% of the monsters in Gehennom to death with a +0 Orcish Dagger.
 Yes, I am likely to use magic missile against liches if I have that
spell, but I'm not going out of my way to do uber spell damage because
it is completely unnecessary.  For example, the time I'd spend boosting
my XL to 30 (for the uber spell damage) would be better spent exploring
Gehennom.  It's fairly easy to get a Monk through Gehennom at XL14
using primarily martial arts damage, so I really don't see any reason
why I should boost my damage ridiculously high, just so I can overkill
monsters.



